  "discreet": ["The counselor was famously discreet; in thirty years she never revealed a single detail of what her clients told her.", "這位輔導員以謹慎低調聞名；三十年來，她從未透露客戶告訴她的任何一個細節。"],
  "vigilant": ["Because the disease could return without warning, doctors remained vigilant, monitoring patients closely for months after the outbreak seemed to end.", "由於這種疾病可能毫無預警地復發，醫生們保持警覺，在疫情看似結束後仍密切監測病患長達數月。"],
  "deliberate": ["Unlike her hasty predecessor, the new editor was deliberate, spending weeks considering every proposal before committing the magazine to a direction.", "與她倉促的前任不同，新任編輯深思熟慮，在決定雜誌方向前會花數週考慮每一項提案。"],
  "meticulous": ["The meticulous restorer spent three years cleaning the mural, removing grime one square centimeter at a time so no paint was lost.", "這位一絲不苟的修復師花了三年清理壁畫，每次只清除一平方公分的污垢，以免損失任何顏料。"],
  "scrupulous": ["The historian was scrupulous about sources, refusing to cite any claim she could not trace back to an original document.", "這位歷史學家對資料來源極為嚴謹，拒絕引用任何無法追溯到原始文件的說法。"],
  "punctilious": ["The punctilious host insisted that every place card be aligned and every fork set exactly two centimeters from the plate.", "這位拘泥細節的主人堅持每張座位卡都要對齊，每把叉子都要放在距離盤子正好兩公分的位置。"],
  "fastidious": ["A fastidious editor, he would return a manuscript over a single misplaced comma, unwilling to tolerate even minor imperfections.", "身為一位挑剔的編輯，他會因為一個放錯位置的逗號就退回稿件，連細小的瑕疵都無法容忍。"],
  "foolhardy": ["Climbing the peak without ropes during a storm was not brave but foolhardy, a risk no experienced mountaineer would ever take.", "在暴風雨中不用繩索攀登那座山峰並非勇敢，而是魯莽，任何有經驗的登山者都不會冒這種險。"],
  "temerity": ["The junior researcher had the temerity to interrupt the Nobel laureate mid-lecture, a breach of etiquette that shocked the audience.", "這位資淺的研究員竟冒失地在諾貝爾獎得主演講途中打斷他，這種失禮行為令聽眾震驚。"],
  "rash": ["The rash decision to sell the company's patents in a single afternoon, without consulting any advisers, cost investors millions.", "在一個下午內、未諮詢任何顧問就賣掉公司專利的輕率決定，讓投資人損失了數百萬元。"],
  "reckless": ["Ignoring every safety warning, the reckless developer built towers on unstable soil, and several cracked within a year.", "這名魯莽的開發商無視所有安全警告，在不穩固的土壤上興建大樓，結果其中幾棟在一年內就出現裂縫。"],
  "heedless": ["Heedless of the critics who warned the plot was too complex, the novelist added three more subplots in the final draft.", "這位小說家不理會評論家說情節過於複雜的警告，在定稿中又加入了三條支線。"],
  "impetuous": ["An impetuous young officer, he charged ahead without waiting for orders, leaving his unit exposed and confused.", "這位衝動的年輕軍官沒有等待命令就率先衝鋒，讓他的部隊暴露在危險中、陷入混亂。"],
