  "audacious": ["The architect's audacious plan to suspend a museum over the river struck many as impossible, yet it was completed on schedule.", "這位建築師要將博物館懸吊在河面上的大膽計畫，在許多人看來根本不可能，但它卻如期完工。"],
  "intrepid": ["The intrepid explorers pressed deeper into the uncharted caves, undeterred by flooding tunnels and failing lamps.", "這些無畏的探險家不顧淹水的隧道和快熄滅的燈，繼續深入未經探勘的洞穴。"],
  "timorous": ["The timorous student, afraid of being wrong, never raised her hand, even when she clearly knew the answer.", "這位膽小的學生害怕答錯，從不舉手，即使她明明知道答案。"],
  "diffident": ["Though his research was groundbreaking, the diffident scientist spoke so hesitantly at conferences that few people noticed his findings.", "儘管他的研究具開創性，這位缺乏自信的科學家在研討會上說話卻如此遲疑，以致很少人注意到他的發現。"],
  "trepidation": ["The villagers awaited the floodwaters with trepidation, knowing the old levee had failed twice before.", "村民們惶恐地等待洪水到來，因為他們知道那道舊堤防以前已經潰堤過兩次。"],
  "apprehensive": ["Apprehensive about the upcoming merger, many employees quietly updated their résumés in case their positions were eliminated.", "許多員工對即將到來的合併感到憂慮，悄悄更新了履歷，以防自己的職位被裁撤。"],
  "perfunctory": ["The inspector gave the bridge only a perfunctory glance before signing the report, missing the cracks a careful check would have revealed.", "檢查員只是敷衍地看了橋一眼就簽了報告，因而漏掉了仔細檢查就能發現的裂縫。"],
  "cursory": ["A cursory reading of the contract suggested it was fair, but closer study revealed several clauses that heavily favored the landlord.", "草率地讀過這份合約，會覺得它很公平，但仔細研究後就發現有好幾條條款大幅偏袒房東。"],
  "negligent": ["The negligent caretaker forgot to lock the gallery for a week, and several valuable prints disappeared during that time.", "這名疏忽的管理員連續一週忘記鎖上美術館，期間有好幾幅珍貴版畫不翼而飛。"],
  "complacent": ["After years of easy victories, the team grew complacent and stopped training hard, only to lose to a far weaker rival.", "在多年輕鬆獲勝後，這支隊伍變得自滿而不再努力訓練，結果輸給了一個弱得多的對手。"],
  "discretion": ["The judge used her discretion to reduce the sentence, deciding that the unusual circumstances justified leniency the law did not require.", "法官運用她的判斷力減輕刑期，認為這種特殊情況值得給予法律並未要求的寬容。"],
  "canny": ["The canny merchant bought grain cheaply before the drought was widely predicted, then sold it when shortages drove prices up.", "這位精明謹慎的商人在乾旱被廣泛預測前低價購入穀物，等到短缺推高價格時再賣出。"],
  "guarded": ["When asked about the company's future, the spokesperson gave only guarded answers, careful not to promise anything specific.", "被問及公司前景時，發言人只給出有所保留的謹慎回答，小心不做出任何具體承諾。"],
  "leery": ["Having been burned by previous fads, investors were leery of the new technology until it showed real profits.", "投資人曾在以往的熱潮中吃過虧，因此對這項新技術抱持戒心，直到它展現真正的獲利。"],
  "skittish": ["The skittish deer bolted at the faintest sound, making the wildlife photographer's job nearly impossible.", "這些易受驚的鹿一聽到最微弱的聲響就逃竄，讓野生動物攝影師的工作幾乎無法進行。"],
  "tentative": ["The two nations reached a tentative agreement, but both sides stressed that many details remained unsettled and could still change.", "兩國達成了試探性的協議，但雙方都強調許多細節仍未定案，還可能改變。"],
  "reluctant": ["Though reluctant to leave her quiet village, the young physician eventually accepted the city hospital's offer for the sake of her research.", "雖然不情願離開寧靜的村莊，這位年輕醫師最終還是為了研究而接受了城市醫院的聘任。"],
  "loath": ["The professor was loath to change grades once posted, believing that exceptions would invite endless complaints from other students.", "教授不願在成績公布後更改，認為一旦破例，就會招來其他學生無止盡的抱怨。"],
  "averse": ["Averse to risk, the retired teacher kept her savings in government bonds rather than chasing higher returns in stocks.", "這位退休教師不願冒險，把積蓄放在政府公債裡，而不去追求股票的較高報酬。"],
  "precaution": ["As a precaution against data loss, the team backed up every file to two separate servers each night.", "為了預防資料遺失，團隊每晚都把所有檔案備份到兩台不同的伺服器上，作為預防措施。"],
  "prophylactic": ["The clinic offered prophylactic vaccinations to travelers before the outbreak could spread, preventing infection rather than treating it.", "診所在疫情擴散前為旅客提供預防性疫苗接種，以預防感染而非事後治療。"],
  "preempt": ["To preempt criticism of the study, the authors addressed every likely objection in the introduction before reviewers could raise them.", "為了先發制人地化解外界對研究的批評，作者在審稿人提出之前，就已在引言中回應了所有可能的質疑。"],
